const HELP_NEWS = "## 1.161.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- People › List: contacts to and from the phone, as vCard (.vcf) files\n  (#383). On a person's page, ⋯ › Share contact hands them to the phone's\n  share sheet, which offers Add contact, or saves the file. Export people\n  saves everyone in the area as one file. Import contacts reads a .vcf and\n  shows each person as New, Changed or Same; nothing is written before\n  Import. Chrome on Android can also pick straight from the phone's\n  contacts. Name, phone, email, organisation and birthday map to phone::,\n  email::, org:: and birthday::.\n\n## 1.160.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Keys on a line: Shift+Enter opens the notepad (#392). It shows the line\n  and the lines under it in a fixed-width box, with the caret's line and\n  column, and Find and Replace. A sketch drawn there keeps its lines and\n  spaces; the file keeps it in a code fence. Done or Ctrl+Enter saves.\n  Shift+Enter no longer adds a line under the line; Enter after ``` still\n  does.\n\n## 1.159.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Weekly review › Steps: a #meeting on a coming day page that links an\n  active project, on its own line or a line above it, keeps the project\n  off Stuck active projects (#385). Cancelled meetings and meetings that\n  only name people do not count. Once the day has passed with no new to do\n  or waiting for, the project is stuck again with \"Meeting held - process\n  the notes\".\n\n## 1.158.1 - 2026-11-14\n\n- The line menu and toolbar: a line refiled from a day page no longer\n  links to the page it lands on (#384). That link becomes a link back to\n  the day it was written on, and the Refiled: note left on the day leaves\n  it out. Other links stay.\n\n## 1.158.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- The line menu and toolbar: Delete asset deletes a file the line links to\n  in assets/ (#391). It warns first that every link to the file stops\n  working and says how many other lines link to it. The link on the line\n  goes with the file.\n\n## 1.157.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- A page: files dropped on \"+ Click here to write a new line\" (or + New\n  line) are kept in assets/, and each gets a new line with its link, as a\n  drop on a line does (#390).\n\n## 1.156.1 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Vault and sync: loose pages straight in the pages folder no longer hold up\n  the start (#181). They come in by name first and are read after the day,\n  the week and your projects, like notes. On a phone with 650 of them this\n  took two minutes off opening the folder.\n\n## 1.156.0 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Vault and sync: a slow start can be traced (#181). Each step of opening\n  an area is logged with its time: listing the folder, today's page, the\n  week and active work, the other files, the pages made from them and each\n  draw. Vault & sync, More, Check the folder now has Save log, which saves\n  those steps, and how long each file took, to your downloads. The steps\n  also show in the browser console as they happen.\n\n## 1.155.14 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Vault and sync: a new day written while the folder is still being read\n  is no longer lost when the folder comes in (#232). The folder had no page\n  for the day yet, so what was written in this browser's copy was set aside\n  until the whole folder was in. Today was made again, empty, over it, and\n  every line was gone. Now the day written in the copy is taken in at once.\n\n## 1.155.13 - 2026-11-14\n\n- Vault and sync: lines typed while the folder is still being read are no\n  longer lost when it comes in (#232). Until then you write in the copy kept\n  in this browser. The folder took over while you were still typing, and\n  only the page under the cursor was kept: a line written after that on\n  another day or page went nowhere. Now the folder waits until you stop\n  typing, then takes in everything written meanwhile.\n\n## 1.155.12 - 2026-11-13\n\n- Vault and sync: today's page opens much sooner in a big folder (#181).\n  The first read no longer takes in notes, mail and reviews. They are there\n  by file name and read behind the day, with the done and cancelled\n  projects. Where the folder has been read in full on this device before,\n  the day folders and the folders of done and cancelled projects, notes,\n  mail and reviews are listed only after today is drawn. Today's page is\n  opened by its name.\n\n## 1.155.11 - 2026-11-13\n\n- A page: ticking a task done no longer jumps the page up when it has\n  pictures on it. A picture keeps its size while the page is drawn again,\n  so the page stays where it was (#382).\n";
